# 🤖 Build Your First RAG Pipeline

## 📌 Project Overview

This project demonstrates how to build a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline using Python, LangChain, OpenAI API, and FAISS.

Large Language Models (LLMs) can sometimes generate incorrect information, also known as hallucinations. RAG helps reduce this problem by retrieving relevant information from a knowledge base and providing it to the language model as context before generating an answer.

This project compares answers generated with RAG against answers generated without RAG to understand how retrieval improves answer grounding.

## 🎯 Objectives

* Connect a FAISS-based semantic search engine to an OpenAI language model.
* Retrieve the top three relevant document chunks for a query.
* Build a `generate_with_rag(query)` function.
* Build a `generate_without_rag(query)` function.
* Test five queries using a custom knowledge base.
* Compare grounded and ungrounded answers.
* Investigate two cases where RAG still produces incorrect answers.
* Create a RAG system architecture diagram.

